MatchedObjectDescriptor.QualificationSummary:
Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience equivalent to the next lower grade level (GS-06) or pay band in the federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector utilizing a thorough knowledge of management and/or program analysis technical rules, guidelines, regulations and precedents and knowledge of basic objectives and policies governing various management or program operations; to assist with studies, interpret the results and recommend alternative course of action for various programs when precedents are applicable and are based on available factual information. Examples of specialized experience may include:
1) Analyzing inventory data for trends to identify and describe recurring problems contributing to deviations from management goals;
2) Applying basic data gathering methods such as standard interviewing or surveying techniques to collect various types of factual information;
3) Identifying inventory problems from collected data and selecting solutions from alternatives in guidelines and precedent cases;
4) Preparing clear, concise reports that describe the data collection techniques and other processes used to recommend improvements. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management website:
https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.
